[INVARIANT]
UID: INV-VOCABULARIES-UNBOUNDED
TITLE: Two declared-bounded vocabularies are unbounded in practice
DEPTH: interface-settled
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
The grain rule labels: 127 rules across 90 distinct labels, one placeholder
appearing 22 times, and case-variant duplicates. The corpus names this a blocker
for a typed model and leaves it open. The cast kind column: declared as ten
values, 43 observed, including multi-word phrases. Nothing in the corpus notices
the second one.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Neither should become a SingleChoice on conversion. The grain vocabulary
dissolves entirely if rules bind to a mechanism by edge rather than by label.
<<<
